From 2b4765446ad91f03c3c8e8833868fba899cfbde3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ObeseCatLord <6099645+ObeseCatLord@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 11:56:06 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] ga2: texture palettes, icon fitting, stacked mods, audio
 queue counters

- gs_texpacks: palettes come from the CPU GS backend's CLUT buffer
  (gs_clut_snapshot.h) unless TEX0 reloads them (then from CBP), so 4-bit
  textures using CSA slices of a loaded 256-colour CLUT decode correctly;
  button icons are fitted by their visible bounds.
- Disc mods: GA2_MODS takes several roots (";", highest priority first).
- Audio: the PCM queue counts underruns; GA2_PERF prints queue level,
  underruns and drops every 5 s.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
